{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKvFiw5gsjY5yfWCh1Cx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #142 as `done` and wrote the result to `.ard/142/triage-lead.md`. The engineer triage role will plan it and the engineer worker will implement it.\n\n- **The request:** when a worker changes any `.gitattributes` file, a human must see it before it can hide files in the GitHub diff. `docs/proposal.md` must also name the rule.\n- **Scope:** the change stays in Go code (the code-path check in `internal/committer/codepath.go`, or the merge hold logic) and the proposal document. That's why the engineer is the only triage role needed. No architect, designer or product-manager role exists in `.ard/triage/` anyway.\n- **Reviewers:** none added. `eng-review` has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it already runs on every pull request.\n\nI flagged two things for maintainers in the file:\n1. **Agent reviewers already see hidden changes.** They get a raw text diff that ignores `.gitattributes` (`internal/gitx/review.go`, `internal/reviewer/doc.go`). What's left is the collapsed diff humans see on GitHub.\n2. **One of the issue's options needs a person.** It suggests adding `.gitattributes` to `merge.protected_paths` in `.ard/config.yaml`. Agents may not edit that file, so if maintainers prefer that over a code-level hold, someone has to make that change by hand."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":761,"cache_read_input_tokens":11645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":761},"output_tokens":468,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9119c9b-df28-4b38-a713-fbad10f46222","uuid":"643d1d0c-6de1-4b24-9aee-50e2b53f9b41","t